✅ Django Basic & Architecture (MVT / MVC)

1. What is Django? Why is it called a high-level web framework?
- Django is a Python web framework that provides many built-in features like ORM, admin, authentication.
- It’s called high-level because it handles most things automatically, reducing developer effort.

2. Explain MVC architecture. How is it different from MVT in Django?

✔ MVC Architecture (Model–View–Controller)

MVC is a popular design pattern used for building web applications.
It separates an application into three components:

Model
- Represents the data and business logic.
- Interacts with the database.

View
- Represents the UI or what the user sees.
- Displays data from the Model.

Controller
- Acts as a bridge between Model and View.
- Handles user input and decides which View to show.
- Controls the flow of the application.

In simple words:
Model = Data
View = UI
Controller = Request handling and application logic

✔ MVT Architecture in Django (Model–View–Template)

Django follows MVT, which is very similar to MVC, but with small changes:

Model
- Same as MVC
- Handles database interactions.

View
- Contains the business logic.
- Processes request and returns response.
- Works like a "Controller" in MVC.

Template
- The HTML part (UI).
- Used to display data to the user.

Important difference:
👉 Django handles the "Controller" part automatically using its URL Dispatcher and framework internals.
So in MVT, we do not manually write a Controller.

✔ Key Differences: MVC vs MVT (Interview Table Format)

| MVC                                                                  | MVT (Django)                                                   |
| -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Has Model, View, Controller                                          | Has Model, View, Template                                      |
| Controller handles user input and communication between Model & View | Django automatically handles controller work using URL routing |
| View = UI                                                            | Template = UI                                                  |
| Developer writes the Controller                                      | Developer writes Views only (no controller needed)             |
| Common in frameworks like Laravel, Spring, Rails                     | Used only in Django                                            |



✔ Interview-Short Answer (30 seconds)
- “MVC consists of Model, View, and Controller.
- Django follows MVT, which is almost similar, but instead of a Controller, Django uses a Template and handles the controller part internally. 
- In MVT, the View contains the business logic, the Model manages data, and the Template handles presentation. 
- The main difference is that Django automatically manages the controller, so developers write only Models, Views, and Templates.”

