3. What are Models, Views, and Templates in Django?

Model → Database structure
View → Business logic
Template → HTML UI

4. What is the role of urls.py in the MVT structure?

It maps incoming URLs to their respective view functions.

✅ Virtual Environment & System Environment
5. What is a virtual environment? Why do we use it in Django projects?

A virtual environment isolates project dependencies and avoids version conflicts.

6. Which command is used to create and activate a virtual environment in Windows/Linux?

Create → python -m venv env
Activate Windows → env\Scripts\activate
Activate Linux → source env/bin/activate

7. What happens if we don’t use a virtual environment for Django development?

Different projects may conflict due to package/version mismatches.

✅ Django Installation & Commands
8. Which command is used to install Django?

pip install django

9. What is the command to create a new Django project?

django-admin startproject projectname

10. How do you create a new Django app?

python manage.py startapp appname

11. Why do we run the command python manage.py makemigrations and migrate?

makemigrations → prepares database changes
migrate → applies those changes to the database

✅ URL Mapping – path & include
12. What is the use of path() in Django?

It maps a specific URL to a view.

13. Why do we use include() in urls.py?

To include app-level URLs and keep the project modular.

14. Can we have multiple urls.py files in a project? If yes, how?

Yes, each app can have its own urls.py, and the main urls.py includes them.

✅ HTTP Response, Render, Redirect
15. What is HttpResponse and when do we use it?

HttpResponse returns plain text or data without using templates.

16. What is render()? Why is it used?

render() loads an HTML template and sends data from the view.

17. What is redirect()? When should we use it instead of render()?

redirect() sends the user to another URL, usually after form submissions or CRUD operations.

✅ Templates & Static Files
18. How do you configure a templates folder in Django?

Add the templates folder path inside TEMPLATES['DIRS'] in settings.py.

19. How do you configure static files in Django?

Set STATIC_URL and STATICFILES_DIRS in settings.py.

20. What are static files? Give examples.

Files not generated dynamically → CSS, JS, Images.

✅ Django Template Language (DTL)
21. What is the purpose of {% extends %} in templates?

To inherit a base template.

22. What is {% block %} and why do we use it?

To define editable sections in templates.

23. What is {% include %} in Django templates?

Used to include reusable components like navbar/footer.

24. What is {% load static %} and when do we use it?

Used to load static files like CSS, JS, images.

25. How do you write an if condition and for loop in Django templates?

If → {% if condition %} ... {% endif %}
For → {% for i in data %} ... {% endfor %}

26. What is the use of context in the render() function?

To pass data from view to template.

