Model.objects.get(id=1).delete()

✅ API & Django REST Framework — CRUD API
35. What is an API?

An API allows two systems to communicate.

36. What is Django REST Framework (DRF) and why is it used?

DRF is used to build APIs easily with serializers, authentication, and API views.

37. What is a Serializer in DRF?

Converts Django objects to JSON and JSON to Python data.

38. Difference between Serializer and ModelSerializer.

Serializer → fields defined manually
ModelSerializer → fields auto-generated from model

39. What is APIView?

A class-based view for handling API requests like GET, POST, PUT, DELETE.

40. What are GET, POST, PUT, DELETE methods used for in API?

GET → Read
POST → Create
PUT → Update
DELETE → Remove

41. What is Postman and why do we use it?

A tool to test APIs.

42. Explain how to create a CRUD API for a To-Do project using DRF.

Create model → create serializer → create API view → add URLs → test in Postman.

43. How do you test API endpoints using Postman?

Choose method → enter URL → add data → send → check response.

44. If a POST request is failing, how do you debug it?

Check serializer errors, required fields, JSON body, and server logs.
